   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Samsung microwave runs, light on, plate turns, fan going, but the food comes out stone cold. Watched a YouTube video on testing the magnetron - I've got the cover screws out already, what should I check first?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't guide any testing or work inside a microwave — the high-voltage capacitor can hold a lethal charge even when it is unplugged, so the casing should only be opened by a qualified engineer. Check the microwave turntable motor and the glass tray to ensure they are rotating correctly during operation. If the food is not turning, inspect the roller ring underneath for damage or debris that might be preventing movement. From what you have checked, this needs an appliance engineer to look at it: the next steps are beyond the checks that are safe to do yourself.\n[Safety panel] Don't remove the microwave's casing or try to repair it inside. Parts inside a microwave can hold a dangerous electric charge even after it's unplugged — have it checked by a qualified engineer."
  }
